Objective Brief
Cosmic Council (cosmiccouncil.chat) is evolving into a companionship-first platform while retaining its advanced astrology capabilities across Council, Apps, and Reports.
This phased plan transforms the Companions module from static V1 presets into Companion Architecture V2, while removing the birth-chart prerequisite from companion conversations and living user memory:
Companionship Without Birth Charts: Users with or without birth charts receive full companion conversations and persistent Living User Context (stored at the user level, independent of public.profiles), with user-facing memory inspection, editing, and deletion.
Relevant & Welcomed Astrology Only: When a user does have a birth chart, Spiritual Guides wait for relevance or invitation before loading or referencing chart/transit payloads—never injecting natal astrology into casual emotional chats merely because a chart exists.
Rich V2 Personality & Lean Runtime: Full personality authoring (essence, fictional lore, inner compass, values, anchors, expression spectrum, contradictions, humor, quirks, linguistic fingerprint, interpersonal dynamics, soft instincts, specialist methodology, and reference dialogues) paired with a soft-target Core Identity Capsule (~500–700 tokens) and conditional nuance/specialist loading so rich texture surfaces even in ordinary chats without prompt bloat.
Governance, Versioning & Portability: Always-active global hard rules with character-specific soft guidance, 'natural' as the default pace cue (instead of 'just_listen'), natural immersion with honest AI identity disclosure when asked, lean Draft / Published / History / Rollback + Core Identity Lock, editable specialization taxonomy across the 65 companions, individual/bulk/global JSON import/export, and an Admin Testing Studio (using /public/assets/aistudio/astra-moon-modern_astrologer-json_576373ab.json as an optional benchmark—without finalizing permanent copy for the 65 companions or global prompts).
Non-Negotiable Constraints (AGENTS.md): Respect #FAF7F2 / #3D3830 Warm Observatory aesthetics, mobile-first 100dvh UX, Cloudflare Workers runtime compatibility, near-zero Supabase egress (no select('*') on heavy JSON columns), zero prompt-leakage via RLS/API responses, and preserve Council, Apps, and Reports intact.
